# Adding Features to FitForge

## New Page / Route

1. Create `src/features/mypage/MyPage.tsx`
2. Use `<AppLayout>` + `<PageHeader>`:
```tsx
import { AppLayout, PageHeader } from '@/components/layout/AppLayout';

export function MyPage() {
  return (
    <AppLayout>
      <PageHeader title="MY PAGE" subtitle="Brief description" />
      <div className="p-6 space-y-6">
        {/* content */}
      </div>
    </AppLayout>
  );
}
```
3. Add import + route in `src/App.tsx`
4. Add to `navItems` in `src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx`
5. Add to `mobileNav` in `src/components/layout/MobileNav.tsx` (keep max 5 items)

## New Training Plan

1. Create `src/data/myPlan.ts` — export object matching `FitnessPlan` type from `gptPlan.ts`
2. Add to `allPlans` in `src/features/plans/PlansPage.tsx`
3. Add to `plans` map in `src/features/plans/PlanDetailPage.tsx`

## New Store Action

Add to the appropriate store (`trackingStore`, `goalsStore`, `userStore`):
```ts
myAction: (param) =>
  set((s) => ({
    myArray: [...s.myArray, { ...param, id: genId() }],
  })),
```

## New Achievement

Add to `defaultAchievements` array in `src/store/goalsStore.ts`:
```ts
{
  id: 'unique_id',
  title: 'Achievement Name',
  description: 'What the user did',
  icon: '🏆',
  category: 'workout' | 'streak' | 'nutrition' | 'weight' | 'steps' | 'consistency',
  requirement: 10,   // target number
  unlocked: false,
  progress: 0,
}
```

## New Habit (default)

Add to `habits` array in initial state of `src/store/goalsStore.ts`:
```ts
{
  id: genId(),
  name: 'Habit Name',
  icon: '🎯',
  color: '#C8FF00',
  targetDaysPerWeek: 5,
  completedDates: [],
  createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
}
```
